  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952: a contest for four aldermanic seats and twelve councillors returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 23 May 1952, p. 10; Londonderry Sentinel, 8 May 1952, p. 3). Five candidates for four aldermanic seats; the outgoing Mayor, S. J. Henry, topped the poll. Murphy is the only successful candidate who was previously an alderman. Labour is the only label printed."
